{"title":"Euclid 2020/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid_2020/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) The positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> have no common divisor larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If the\ndifference between b and a is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9584e7508973e719087ed6c32b4fe56b2b7c1a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac59&lt;\\frac{a}b&lt;\\frac47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />?\n</p><p>(b) A geometric sequence has  first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> .\nAn arithmetic sequence has  first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nThe ratio of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e3218d569b20eb9c4e1b86c362a029f84fe4f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6th$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> term in the geometric sequence to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8f916b1d022f4c6ccbb2f8391870977eb0039a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4th$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> term in the\ngeometric sequence equals the ratio of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e3218d569b20eb9c4e1b86c362a029f84fe4f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6th$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> term in the arithmetic sequence\nto the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8f916b1d022f4c6ccbb2f8391870977eb0039a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4th$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> term in the arithmetic sequence.\nDetermine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n(An arithmetic sequence is a sequence in which each term after the  first is obtained\nfrom the previous term by adding a constant, called the common difference. For\nexample, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f3022d91057132722e97c3310ef385e031a37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3; 5; 7; 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> are the  first four terms of an arithmetic sequence.\nA geometric sequence is a sequence in which each term after the  first is obtained\nfrom the previous term by multiplying it by a non-zero constant, called the\ncommon ratio. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfe6c13c08ce680c19f341ba05a913d3a103d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 6, 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> is a geometric sequence with three terms.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid_2020/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cee4c1bc083c3979f7ac19ac9f8646a3d0a29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbdf54bb2e83a91aeaa4050a8fbdf9847927eeef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> are less than one, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Because the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is 15, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a6a71fe875713aeac9966e202f5dacd27bac50a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2178586798e87e92d8558e23df0f4fd2dee4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac59&lt;\\frac{b-15}b&lt;\\frac47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"39\" />. Using the left side of the equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab698fb803e8eece497bad768aaefc237df31d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac59&lt;\\frac{b-15}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1135c755a43c0a38f0126aed1d125790ef7bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5b&lt;9b-135$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/4421f9e4243894c05e351f2dfbc7ef14103a5d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135&lt;4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7887738b069bfd63aa937d24fda0ced004ef7abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;\\frac{135}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />. Using the right side of the equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6e18df56823df45c1b67e8f927eb101d7b8395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b-15}b&lt;\\frac47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf01f9321095bef6f2afa201a6105a715410f630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7b-105&lt;4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca581a50e35e22225591a3e6e8d43be3ca3b924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b&lt;105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39b277ef46374a012e774ae30855936a456454c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. Combining both inequalities will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e4be0c9751abe0bec1a7ea0ebc9afe1ae04e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35&gt;b&gt;\\frac{135}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />, so the only possible integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b7047aef8012ac1246d0d6a8d01e34ffdcef33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf68cfb8589c373cdcb7658bbd197ddcdc9271e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{19}{34}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>(b) By bashing it out, we have the 4th term of the geometric sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3628e955d7e4a0e6322ada48bc33c003f9b25dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> and the 6th term be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca06360e5e53ef1471b7c7ff1b0bd7b40c5dd88e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />. Because the arithmetic sequence has first term 10 and common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, its 4th term will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8138f49b87ba58eec3a5f26e70a0816ab4b5c896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and its 6th term will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fe0d47c6773435f047f2c5d74e74eaf08bf2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+5d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. Our equation will then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fda15c191db65c25e34be964c9dca07bb2ca449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{5}{16}}{\\frac{5}{4}}=\\frac{10+3d}{10+5d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"110\" height=\"49\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3165810eaeac9b7fc1d92722ba0595f583bb3b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14=\\frac{10+3d}{10+5d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e5d135d2d2a63526d161ddb9f8d0432cb77b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+5d=40+12d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21bcad18a6bcd6c5248b5c5365ce4b2dd6be804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-30=7d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff70d834592905c2abe89bbe3eee8626ffab941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{-30}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f93764e32f60e858c4a0180f8891339083e49a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{-30}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"49\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 180/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8435/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24188:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018083801 and revision id 285372. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}